You got that right.  We run numerical water resources models...a year
ago were seriously considering abandoning our Sparc computers
(price/performance wasn't there) and wanted to benchmark an Alpha.
Digital didn't have a demo machine we could log into for a couple of
days over the Internet (were very proud in fact of their bulletproof
firewall), and wanted us to sign an agreement to pay for an inhouse
loaner if I broke it.  Not necessarily unreasonable,..but not flexible
enough either.  It always amazes me how companies can discourage
customers who call them basically asking to do business.  Anyway we
used that year's money to buy PPro machines to try NT...another
disappointment. This year we're back to Sparcs, especially since Sun
offers great tradein deals.  While the Sparc performance may not match
the Alpha, at least the price/performance is a lot better than a year
ago.  Oh yeah--a few months ago Sun loaned us a machine to benchmark,
no agreements to sign.  Two weeks ago they ftp'd our codes, ran them,
benchmarked them, no hassle to us.  As a result of those numbers we
completely changed our original thinking away from a single server and
are going to upgrade all our old desktop machines.





