Peter Reuter wrote:
> command 'mount -r -o noversion -t cdfs /dev/rz4c /cdrom'
> gets a response 'No such device /dev/rz4c /cdrom'

I guess you need to re-build the kernel with CDFS support. Edit the file
/sys/conf/MACHINE to include the line 'options CDFS' and use the command
'doconfig -c MACHINE' (or use 'doconfig' without options, and select CDFS
from the menu), then replace /vmunix and reboot. (Hope this helps.)

