In article <6fobis$eit$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>,  <zap_25@hotmail.com> wrote:
>Hello everyone,
>
>I recently got my hands on a decstation.
>Ultrix was already installed and I was
>told I could run X-windows on it.
>Now the problem is that there is a version
>installed but someone messed up a config
>file so it won't run.
>
>Can anyone tell me where I can find the
>config files (I don't know how much there
>are but I figure that when I know the
>directory I can check the dates on the
>files that were accessed most recently)

Just look for the most recently modified files--
the trashed one will be one of the few just 
before all the system-modified files.

I resurrected a non-booting Sun 3/50 (wouldn't
go multiuser) by doing basically this--it was
given to me, and the previous owner was able
to tell me roughly when was the last time it
worked. So I went looking for files dated
around that time, and found one with a bad
console entry. Fixed that, and it booted
right up.

I'd suspect the X config files are under /usr/X11
or something similar, which would cut down on your
searching.


Gary

