}Bob Koehler                     | Computer Sciences Corporation

You should also be sure that you did *not* record using compression on
the 60m tape using the DDS-2 drive. A DDS-1 drive can not read a tape
that was made with compression enabled on the DDS-2 drive.

--- Carl



