I've got a AlphaServer 2100 and configuring it as a file server, with a 
single channel SWXCR RAID controller, connected to the internal
StorageWorks box ( set as a single bus). The original plan was to move the
4 RZ29-VA user disks (mounted on a DEC 3000/700 via ufs & system bd SCSI)
WITHOUT doing the low-level initialization called for in the SWXCR manager
software. The low-level initialization will destroy all the data present
on the disks. The disks are already partitioned & formatted and have data
on them; why reload the info? The 2 "system" disks which were purchased
with the system are RZ29-VW.

Has anyone tried adding disks to a SWXCR controller as JBODs and NOT
initialized them?? I understand that to build RAID devices, you have to do
the low-level initialization or RAID would not work.

When you've completed the setup, you just rebuild the kernel, make the
special files and mount the disks and the data should be fine.

