I'm looking to do some implementations of data structures such as binary trees 
and linked lists in Ada - GNAT and Rational - on boxes running DU4.0x with 
Alpha CPU's. I've spent a lot of time over the last 12 months working with 
performance-critical code on the Alpha. This experience leads me to believe 
that while doing standard data structures is not all that difficult, getting 
their implementation to make full use of the Alpha will be, perhaps, a little 
more challenging. I was wondering if anyone knows of any publicly available 
work describing fast implementations of standard data structures on 
multi-leveled cache, RISC CPU's such as the Alpha. Or maybe someone has heard 
of a commercial API/STL which is genuinely optimised for the Alpha.

