In article <351674E3.DFCB6CF5@zam360.zam.kfa-juelich.de>, "he.ziegler" <zdv092@zam360.zam.kfa-juelich.de> writes:
|>hi,
|>i need a more accurate description of the performance counting abilities
|>of the 21164. I am reffering to
|>the pages 87 ff. in the "Alpha 21164 Microprocessor Data Sheet"
|>(EC-QAEPC-TE).

But that description is perfectly accurate - there is no more to it. You can
also look at the 21164 Hardware Reference Manual (EC-QAEQB-TE) which is also
available on the web.

Basically you turn on the performance counter stuff using a bit in the
ICSR (p5-20 et seq. in the HRM). The counters then count and (if enabled)
interrupt according to the setting of PMCTR. The interrupt will be handled
by the PALcode and passed on to the OS accordingly.

