Terry Shannon wrote:
> 
> Assume a soft-partitioned WildFire-class system with 32 CPUS. Half are
> running WNT on little-endian IA64, half are running, say HP-UX on
> big-endian IA64. I do not believe it would be possible to dynamically
> reallocate CPUs from the WNT side of the box to the HP-UX side of the
> box because of the disparate byte ordering of the respective OS/CPU
> pairs.

I would have expected part of the sequence of events when switching a
CPU from one node to another would be a power-off-on-cycle-equivalent 
re-set, in order to be sure that it came into the new node in a known 
state, and to avoid the improper transfer of information out of a 
secure node.  That should provide an adequate opportunity for endianness
switching. 

