The help pages for popen look like this...

CC

  Run-time_functions

    popen

       Initiates a pipe to a process.

       Syntax:

             #include <stdio.h>

             FILE *popen (const char *command, const char *type);


As you can see the only header file it's requiring is stdio.h.

The program itself

$ type new.c
#include <stdio.h>

void main()
{
        FILE *fi;
        FILE *popen();
        int pclose();
        fi = popen("PMDF MAIL", "w");
        fprintf(fi, "send\n");
        fprintf(fi, "lakha001@cerritos.edu\n\n");
        fprintf(fi, "This is a test\n");
        fprintf(fi, "Mail sent using C program\n");
        fprintf(fi, "^Z\n");
        pclose(fi);
}
$ CC/DECC/PREFIX_LIBRARY_ENTRIES=ALL_ENTRIE
$ link new
