Having just checked this out recently for someone, I can
tell you that the documentation specifically states that
the I/O page is 8kb (4kw), no mention at all of being
able to have it set 4kb (2kw).

To check this out, I installed an 11/83 board with an MSV11-D
memory board jumpered for bank7 response.  MAP showed memory
from 000000-177776.  When I booted SB, top of memory was
160000.  I installed the patch to allow booting as high as
170000 and tried rebooting... top of memory was still 160000.

>I am aware that it should be possible to have the CPU
>run with a 2 KWord I/O Page, but I do not understand
>what I must do.  Can an 11/73 in a 22 bit backplane
>invoke a 2 KWord I/O Page?  Or is this situation
>reserved for only an 11/23?  Or must a 16 bit backplane
>be used (or at the most an 18 bit backplane like in a
>BA-11 box)?

Keep in mind that even with an 11/23, if you enable
memory management the I/O page reverts (in hardware) to
8kb (4kw).  It is probable that with the DCJ chip, this
restriction was extended to all times, not just when the
memory mapping is turned on.

I also tried disabling the 11/83 ROM code which starts
at 165000, but to no avail.

