        Yep, wasting perfectly good  cycles  on  WNT  and UNIX.  :-) :-)

        Call me dense, but I  really  have a hard time understanding the
    advantage  of  running  several O/S's in one box.   I've  heard  the
    market-speak about "migrating from one O/S to another" while keeping
    the same hardware, and I'll even admit that there are  cases  of  an
    application that runs on unix but not VMS, and vice versa, for which
    you  need to support multiple O/S's.  I could even imagine, vaguely,
    wanting to use Galaxy software  to  migrate cpu and memory resources
    dynamically  amongst  several dissimilar systems, but  you  wouldn't
    share disks that way (file system structure is  too  different)  and
    I'd  think you'd be putting yourself at risk in several ways if, for
    example, one of the non-VMS O/S's  was  not as robust as it needs to
    be  and  manages to corrupt the locking structures or otherwise  get
    outside is allocated memory or cpu resources...  Ay, Laddie, it's  a
