Given my choice, so would I. OTOH, let's say you've got one box, and one
box only due to floor space or budgetary limitations, whatever. Let's
say that you have mission-critical apps that run on OVMS, but that you
could save big bucks by running other apps in a less-costly environment
such as WNT, or that you could run other apps that are not supported
under OVMS. OS stability and resiliency issues aside, this makes a case
for a mixed-OS environment.
 
