>     additional  software, so much as asking what you would _use_  Galaxy
>     for.  

The only additiona software in a Galaxy is a modest amount of OVMS code,
plus the GUI and console. As to what you would use Galaxy for, you'd use
it for the same things you use OVMS for today (Steve Z's stock trading
demo is a pretty good example of WHY you'd use it).

What's more, flat SMP systems such as TurboLaser don't scale all that
well. Scaling on commercial apps begins to run out of gas somewhere
around 6 or 8 CPUs. Hence, current OVMS won't play that well on a 64-CPU
(or, heaven forbid) a 128- or 256-CPU WildFire-class machine. However, a
64-CPU WildFire equipped with eight 8-CPU instances should provide
reasonably decent scaling. Time will tell.


If I'm correct, the people at Hannover were highly  remiss  in
>     not telling the story!
