A little more information on what you've tried and how it has failed
would be helpful. Basically, you need to add the partition you want to
use for swap in /etc/fstab (see man fstab for guidance). Then 
"swapon -a" will make all swap areas in /etc/fstab available for swap
(see man swapon). This should also retain the swap areas across reboots.
If the 9GB partition you mention is larger than you want, you should
first partition the external disk using "disklabel".
Regards,
John Hill
