>
> I've installed a DEC LN17ps on our LAN.  I've set up a LPR queue
> (via UCX) to print to it, and that works without any problem, as
> long as I don't try to do anything fancy.

Install DECprint Supervisor (DCPS) for more features than are offered
with LPR printing.  The base functionality of DCPS (free) include the
ability to do landscape printing.  DCPS V1.3 and higher support the
LN17ps printer; DCPS V1.4 allows TCP/IP connections to it.

Without DCPS, yes, you need to create a device control library with a
module to send the proper PostScript code or ANSI escape sequences to
set the page orientation to landscape.

