A couple of things.
1. You could use the internal and external connectors at the same time as
long as you follow the SCSI rules absolutely. The big factor is total
cable length. You'd have to add up the interior cable and the exterior
cable lengths and ensure you were within Spec.
2. The intention was to support more than one SCSI card on the PCI bus
originally, but due to some issues that cropped up with timing and
throughput, early tests showed the possibility of data corruption. Thus,
the rules were changed to have only one SCSI card supported. So, that is
why you have the sales person stating the most current information, which
is different that some early documentation you may have. Go with the sales
guy and save the headaches.
3. You could change out the card and go for something else entirely, like
a InterServer 3280 UE or 4280UE or an Adaptec with more than one SCSI
channel.

rtt

