In article <35100268.0@news3.enter.net>, "me" <mozcure@hotmail.com> writes:
|>Hi.....my computer sometimes loses it's IDE...(hey it's a Digital) and I
|>have to go into the reg editor and delete the NOIDE key....other then
|>praying for this problem to be addressed in a bios upgrade is there a quick
|>fix????

This is a problem with the CMD 640 IDE controller chip used on this and many
other PCs of that era.  There's no "fix" other than editing the registry
as you are doing.  The BIOS can't do anything about it.  It appears to
be a problem only if you have an IDE CD-ROM installed.  My Celebris FP590
has the same CMD chip and I never see this problem, but my CD-ROM is SCSI.

If you have a spare slot, you might consider an add-on IDE controller card
and disable the onboard IDE.
