"jlauschke" <jlauschke@premierair.com> writes:
>Have a DDS-1 DAT drive on our development system (MV3100-10e) that gives an
>invalid ansi format error when we try to read a tape from the DDS-2 DAT
>drive on our live system (MV3100-88).  We are running VMS 6.2 on both
>systems and the distributor says they should be compatible as long as I use
>60m tapes.  I am trying to copy the information using the backup command.
>Any help would be much appreciated!!!
>
Most probably the DDS-2 is doing auto-compression (has nothing to do if it is 
60 m tape or longer, but most older drives supporting only 60 m tapes also do 
not have compression). 
Check the manual of the DDS-2 drive. On VMS system some years ago many
vendors configured drives with "auto-compressing", disabling "software 
controlled compression". In a "show device/full" this device appears to not 
support compression, although it silently does. In this case the tape is 
unreadable on the DDS-1 drive.

