>On 14 Mar 1998 18:02:09 GMT, "Aaron Hodgson"

><aaron.hodgson@virgin.net> wrote:

>>Do pci33 Motherboards work with a standard 200W PC power supply?
>>Because I have just imported one from the USA, and when I plug it into
>>my 200W power supply it does not work neither does the PSU, but as
>>soon as I unplug the motherboard from the PSU, the PSU works.

>I hope that you did not insert the power supply cables backwards
>as this usually results in a fried mobo. The black wires on the
>connectors should be 'together' or in the middle. Let's see...

>                connector        connector
>            |---------------||---------------|
>             ----------- ---  --- -----------
>                   |      |    |       |
>various colors ----*      |    |       |
>black---------------------*----*       |
>various colors ------------------------*

	Just so.  That is the 'usual PC motherboard configuration' (at least
	in my observation.)  Also, there are TWO sets of twelve pin PSU
	connectors.  The 5/12/etc (standard psu connector, as above) is the\
	one labeled J32, which is NOT at the edge of the motherboard,

	(J34 is for supply of 3.3vdc to the PCI slots ONLY, and is not
	needed, unless a 3.3v PCI card is used...).  If using J34 IT has
	the grounds at the outer edges, with +3.3v in the 'center'.
	J33 and J34 are keyed differently, however the keying on the PSU
	cables can be overridden...)

