The Prioris XL Server is no more than a "refresh" of the DECpc XL Server
with
a new name, some newer rev chipset pieces, newer rev CPU daughtercard
(with Dual-Proc support), faster processor options and enclosure knock-outs
for external SCSI connectors (from the embedded controller on the
motherboard).

Digital renamed the DECpc XL Server to be more in line with the other
servers
(the same was done to the DECpc MTE which became the Prioris MTE before
the low-end replacement Prioris LX came out; the Prioris XL Server had a
longer
window to live while waiting for the Prioris MX replacement).

I've upgraded a Pentium processor based DECpc XL Server to the latest (at
the time) Prioris XL Server BIOS and everything worked fine and dandy (but
officially DEC probably doesn't support it ;-).

And for the uninitated: The DECpc/Prioris XL Servers are not to be confused
with the DECpc XL workstation which was "refreshed" and became the
Celebris XL. The same enclosure was also used for some Alpha models;
including those where the DECpc XL/Celebris XL Intel CPU daughtercards
could be swapped for an Alpha CPU daughtercard (the "DECpc" variants
usually required also a motherboard upgrade, but it was included in the
price).

regards,
