> Does anyone have any info on opening up an Ultra Hinote (4/75)??
> I just received a new hard drive to upgrade the box and I am
> having trouble figuring out how to open the sucker up!!

Somebody should benefit from the carnage I wrought on my HiNote
Ultra when I performed this kind of upgrade... However, you do
this at your own risk - be aware that you can seriously damage
your laptop by doing this. Now that the legal beagles have been
appeased, on with the show.

If you look at the HiNote Ultra open before you, the keyboard is
set back behind the trackball. The first step is to disengage two
small plastic sliders that keep the keyboard in place. Under the
keyboard are some screws that keep the plastic cover on the unit.
Under this grey/black case material front and center when you're
facing the unit is the disk drive, and replacement is a snap at
that point.

Back to the keyboard. There are these two sliders; one between and
below the left Alt key and space bar, and between/below the left
and down arrow keys on the right side of the keyboard. You want to
use a long thin impliment like a pin or mechanical pencil and
insert it into the hole at the end of the slider away from the
keyboard. Slide these plastic bits away from you, out from under
the case and into the keyboard.

With the sliders back (I think there's only the two) you should be
able to flip the keyboard up, lifting the edge closest to you. Now
go to work on the screws you've exposed. I think that from here
its fairly straightforward.

Good luck,
--Steve.

