Organization: University of Auckland, Tamaki Campus
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Hi everyone,

I am working on a project which deals with the the Evaluation of
prefetching, prefetching algorithms and studying the effectivness
through the performance of some benchmarks.

We have got some problems regarding the prefetch instructions
implementedin the DEC - Alphas.  I would be grateful if any of you could
help me out with answers to my following questions.  I have checked up
the documentation 'Digital' provides at their web sites and the research
sites, but couldn't find any information which could answer my
questions.

Some of the questions which I have are:

1.  Do the prefetch instructions supported by Alpha processors namely
   21064 EV4 running at 166Mhz and 21164 EV5 running at 250Mhz really
   work (i.e. prefetch the data) or the processor ignores them as a
   no-op?

2.  How many outstanding prefetch requests could be existing at a time?

3.  What happens if the prefetch request for the same data is made 
   repeatedly?  Does the processor ignore the request, or prefetches it 
   again?

5.  Is there any kind of a prefetch request buffer, which can hold the
   prefetch requests made but are not yet fulfilled?

4.  What happens when the data needed is already existing in the cache
and there is a prefetch request for it?  Does the processor probe the 
cache or it makes a prefetching request to the memory? 

Thanks in advance, for any information on the above questions.  It
would be really nice if you could mail me the information to my
e-mail address

Shailender
