Matt Callaway wrote:
> I am getting an unexpected error when linking a program. All object
> files are generated using CPP and CC. When I try to link the files, I
> get an object file format error "Bad magic file number".  

It looks like one of the files in your link line is not a valid
object file.  The linker will emit that error message when an 
object file is neither an OMAGIC, an NMAGIC or a ZMAGIC file.  
The ld manpage describes the meaning of those three kinds of files.
The default is ZMAGIC and most users have no reason to change it.

I'd double check to see exactly what is being linked.

Joe Mario
DIGITAL UNIX Development Environment



