Aaron Hodgson (aaron.hodgson@virgin.net) wrote:
: Do pci33 Motherboards work with a standard 200W PC power supply?
: Because I have just imported one from the USA, and when I plug it into
: my 200W power supply it does not work neither does the PSU, but as
: soon as I unplug the motherboard from the PSU, the PSU works.
: 
: Thank You
: 
: Aaron, :o)
: 

There are two plugs on the Axppci33 motherboard which look like the
standard PC case power supply connectors, but one is not what you
think...  The connector which is closer to the PCI slots is the
correct power supply connector....  The other connectro is for
supplying 3.3V to the PCI bus for certain cards.  You need a special
power supply to use this special connector, but if you're not using
any 3.3V PCI cards, then you can just use a standard PC supply (using
the correct connector).  If you need further info, check out the
following URL:

http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/axppci/read_me.html

	good luck,
	dave panofsky <moody@mathworks.com>


