I am sorry that you don't seem to grok the use of "ALT" in the 
source. In properly designed browsers each clickable spot is 
thusly labeled and not just by the latest version of lynx. "ALT" 
is supported by every character only browser.  Some people have 
hacked up graphical browsers to take the place of character browsers 
and sometimes those hacks don't fully support html (ie "ALT"). 
To blame the company that produces the web page is a failure to 
take responsibility and to put out a flame telling people that 
the page is broken when it is your browser that is bust, is not
nice.
 
> 
> : PS It is not "covered by a client-side imagemap"
> 
> While strictly true (there is a link to "Legal"), this statement
> is very misleading.  If you don't have a browser that can handle
> client-side imagemaps, then you're out of luck.

It is true in several senses. First and formost there is *no*
client-side image map covering the page. There are several discreet
images and each one has an "ALT" reference. If someone has a text
only browser then they see the following:

_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_

                                                  DIGITAL: Quash

                 Hand All rumors aside, here are the facts.
                             Q | U | A | S | H
                                   Bottom
                             Bottom Navigation
                                  [INLINE]
                             DIGITAL Navigation
                                  [INLINE]
                                   Legal


_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_

As they work their way into the site they see similar things.

Charlie

PS If Jonathan had said that his noncompliant browser couldn't 
handle the web site instead of posting that the page was broken and
had explained *accurately* why... oh well water under the bridge.

PPS DEC gets enough 'flack' for stuff that they really did wrong,
lets try not to bust their chops when they really did not foul up!

