|>
|>Does it have a very long initialization (compared to GPX) which
|>means I just didn't wait long enough for a picture? GPX quite
|>quickly starts to display test pictures in the same machine,
|>while this board just flickered the screen.

This is a definite possibility.

For a number of years I ran a VS3100-76 with SPX and it was (or felt like)
several minutes between powering on and seeing *anything* on the monitor.

Then you get a brief flash of a "cross" followed by a few seconds of 
blank screen and finally the self-test starts to appear on the monitor. And
then you sit and wait another minute or so in test ..B while 32MB or RAM is
checked and checked and checked.

But I'm not complaining - it ran 24x7 for over two years with an annual
power down for building maintenance and one hardware failure when things
got to hot one summer (and the building air-conditioning failed).

