: Help!
: 
: I recently purchased an AXPpci33 MB.  Installed in a clone case with a
: Trident ISA VGA card; 1.44 FD; 1.0 GB IDE Seagate HDD; 2 70 NS SIMMS;
: noname VGA monitor.  Quick and dirty just to see it work..
: 
: I turned it on; hear the drive spin; and then -- nothing!  No output to
: the display.  Has anyone traveled this path before and fixed it?

First off, you may not be waiting long enough...  The motherboard runs
through some diagnostics and takes over 30sec to initialize the video
card.  Secondly, you must be using true parity memory.  The behavior
you're describing is exactly hoy my Axppci33 acted when I had the
wrong sort of memory installed.  

	Good Luck
