In article <6e5o65$s3t$1@sunnews.cern.ch>, becchett@na48s01.cern.ch (Enrico Becchetti) writes:
>How can I update firmware ,on some DEC HUB 900 family modules,
>if TFTP metod doesn't work ? After some attempt my PEswitch900
>can't load new firmware from any tftp server (I've tried with hp-ux
>and linux). Any ideas ??

TFTP is the only supported method for transferring the load image into the hub
NVRAM (besides buying a new module with a new firmware).

But initiating the image download can be done with
	- a terminal (emulator) on the HUB console port
	- DECndu on OpenVMS (uses its own TFTP server)
	- DECndu on PC (I'm not sure on that)
	- ClearVISN Hubloader on Win32 (uses its own TFTP server)
	- handmade SNMP SETs with a general SNMP manager tool (eg. SPECTRUM)

