Hi all,

I recently purchased a Digital HiNote VP562 with the intention of
loading Windows NT Workstation on it, which I have just done.

Needing a network & modem card, I found the Xircom CreditCard Ethernet
10/100+Modem56 seemed to do what I want -- especially as it does GSM
too.  This card is otherwise known as a CEM56.

However, I can't get the thing to work!  Here's what happened.

I installed WNT (Build 1381, SP1) which went OK.  However, I soon worked
out that NT didn't recognise the PCMCIA adapter, which I fixed by
loading Cardwizard 3.00.08 at Digital's recommendation.  Now the system
recognises the PCMCIA adapter, and the Cardwizard software detects the
presence of the Xircom card.

However, the Xircom card doesn't start up.  Cardwizard reports "A
general network error has occurred in attempting to install the chosen
card.  You may attempt to reinsert the card to correct the problem."

Looking in Event Viewer I find the following events:

6:34:05PM  CEM56 reports "Unable to identify the adapter."
6:34:05PM  Service Control Manager reports "The Xircom CreditCard
           10/100+Modem 56 service failed to start due to the following
           error: A device attached to the system is not functioning."
6:34:25PM  Above 2 entries repeated.


So the Xircom card doesn't appear to be able to talk to CardWizard's
PCMCIA driver.

The initial response from Xircom is to use CardWizard V4 but Digital say
it's not available for this machine.

Does anyone know of a way of getting this setup working?  Please EMAIL
your responses to jeremy@vsm.com.au.

