Greetings all,
We are in the process of trying to come up with a solution whereby
remote users can access the console of a couple of DEC Alpha 2100
servers.  This will be used for out of band management.

I have been told that doing this may cause the alpha serves to crash
when the terminal sessions are brought down.  The reason I was given
is that if the session goes down, the server will continue to try and
write data to the terminal, eventually overloading a buffer and
crashing the servers.  The solution I have been told, is to use a
device to "fool" the server into thinking that the session is always
up, by crossing the rts and cts pins.

I have also been told that DEC makes such a device.

The questions are:
1. Do DEC servers crash when hooked to a terminal server?
2. If so, does anyone know where to find one of these cross-over
devices?
3. Does anyone have the pin-outs for a DEC console connection?

Thanks in advance, please respond via e-mail to ilazar@rpm.com

Thanks,
Irwin


