  VT1300 X-terminal typically would use Vaxeln based X-terminal software
called EWS. I
do not know whether EWS is still available. The last version (that I
know) is V1.2 and this
version supports OpenVMS VAX / Ultrix VAX /  Ultrix Mips.

In fact the software is installed in the host system (in your case host
system would be linux).
The VT1300 boots stuff from host using MOP (perhaps BOOTP works also
though I never
used it to load VT1300). And then VT1300 connects to EWSdaemon on the
host over
DECnet  or over TCPIP. EWSdaemon on the host launches X-window login
sequence typically.

The stuff that runs on the host never got ported to Digital Unix Alpha
or OpenVMS Alpha. And
it never was available on anything else but OpenVMS VAX/Ultrix
VAX/Ultrix MIPS as far as
I know.

VT1300 can also use VXT software but to use VXT on the VT1300 you would
need Infoserver with VXT support on your LAN.

If you somewhere VAX and you have VAXeln runtime kit, maybe you could
build a custom image
to be downlineloaded to your VT1300. Or maybe, since EWS software has
been End of Life at least
a couple of years, DEC could be persuaded to put the stuff on the
freeware CD...

