Looking at the manual, the default is for it to auto-sense an external cable,
and disable the internal termination if one is detected.

But you can disable this feature by fitting jumper J21 on the motherboard (in
which case, an external terminator is needed, even with no external devices
present).

Don't have an AS200 to hand, only the manual, so I don't know if the jumper is
lebelled on the MB. If you look at the board with the CPU to the front/left, the
jumper would be towards the rear, very close to the left edge.

Graham



