Phillip Helbig <helbig@multivac.jb.man.ac.uk> wrote:
: I've inherited three DECserver 2000/MC.  I would appreciate some brief 
: information on what I can do with them!  (I'm pretty sure I can put them 
: to use; I'm interested in the basic technical details, compatibility 
: issues etc.)

I think you're talking about the DECserver 200/MC, not 2000/MC, right ?
These are terminal servers with 8 RS-232 ports and one AUI ethernet port.
The serial ports can handle speeds up to 38400 bps IIRC, the /MC has
modem control lines. The only protocol the 200/MC understands is LAT,
you can't use it with standard TCP/IP telnet (unless someone manages to
find the guys who ported some 7th Edition Unix to that beast ...). You
will also need a bootimage for it which is booted via the MOP protocol.

Technically speaking, the 200/MC has a Motorola 68000 CPU, 384 or 512 kB
RAM, eight Signetics 2681 UARTs and an AMD LANCE ethernet controller. 

We had a couple 200/MC's (and also the version without the modem control
lines) running here at Siegen Univ. with lots of VT320's attached to it when 
our old VAX8830 was still running. Except for occasionally dying VT320's, we
had lots less trouble than with the NT PC's that replaced the terminals ...

regards,
	Michael Engel	(engel@unix-ag.uni-siegen.de)




