In article <6dj6be$s51$1@sunnews.cern.ch>, becchett@unipg.it (Enrico
Becchetti) wrote:

> Hi all, I've some problems with my LN17 Postscript.
> When I print Ps files on this printer, it doesn't 
> print all page but prints just a part of it. This problem
> appeare when I try to print PS with some picture(eps)
> and when these ps is large (about > 4-5 MB). I bougth 
> 20MB of ram on my LN17, without any improvement.

Try turning Page Protection on.  Otherwise, the LN17 uses a "banding"
technology that starts the engine printing the page before it's completely
composed by the CPU.  If the page is complex, the CPU can't keep up with
the engine and you will get only a partial page of output.  Setting page
protection on ensures that the entire page has been composed before
sending it to the engine.

> Do you konw if there are some possibilities to print
> on LN17 Postscript level 3 files ?

Neither the LN17ps nor the new LN17+ps will print PostScript Level 3 files.

