struct@netcom.com (Patrick Roberts) writes:

> 2)  Is there a way in either NT or Linux to write directly to the screen 
> memory - i.e. Is the video ram mapped to a physical address? (Like Amiga)?

Under Linux and XFree, I believe this is what DGA (Direct Graphics
Access) does.  Running Quake on older (pre-21164) alphas, this option
actually slowed things down, due to having to do byte operations (256
colors). 

There's also an effort called GGI, which aims at providing direct access 
to the graphics hardware in a safe manner, and there's fbcon/vgacon,
which also might do what you want.

The last two (or at least GGI) are quite beta at the moment, and not in
the mainstream kernel tree, but they are discussed extensively on the
linux-kernel list.

