As I recall, the external SCSI port is "auto terminated", meaning that
you don't have to put a terminator on it if you have no external
devices. You shouldn't have to do anything special to hook up an
external device, other than terminate the external end of the SCSI bus.
You also have to make sure to terminate the internal segment of the SCSI
bus. Normally, this is done by setting the appropriate jumpers on the
last internal device.
