1) What is the size of int (sizeof(int)) on an Alpha system running
    Windows NT?

If it is 32-bits or 4-bytes, what is the result of the following
operation?

    int i = 0x80000000;  /* left most bit alone set */
    int j;

    j = i << 1;                /* left shift i by 1 */

What is the value of j?

Since Alpha is a 64-bit architecture and since it does not
support 32-bit shifts (Alpha has only 64-bit shift instructions),
does the compiler mask the upper 4 bytes using extra instructions?
This would seem expensive.  If the size of int is always
8 bytes, this problem does not arise.

2) Is the size of int different on Unix systems on Alpha?

Thanks for your help.

Sivaram





