1.  The error "cannot open display" is usually in response
    to one of the following;

       a) Not having the X-Server (such as eXceed or Reflections/X)
          running on the local PC
        
       b) Not doing an xhost+ (if you are on Unix) from the appropriate
          session (admittedly, I do not remember the command on
          VMS...)
       c) Not having the path to the X binaries in your path so that
          you may run them...
       d) Not having the security permissions required under VMS
          to actually create a socket.
       e) Not have the actual group membership for your VMS UID
          such that you can execute the files for the X client
          app or the X server...

