> 
	Like when did you have a VMS problem that this solved?

>  $ set display/create/transport=tcpip/host=172.21.100.125:0.0

That :0.0 means Display 0 Screen 0 on a UNIX environment variable
eg	DISPLAY=172.21.100.125:0 or 
	setenv DISPLAY 172.21.100.125:0.0


This /node= is not UNIX , this is not an environment variable
to which you append :0.0 (btw I was wrong its /node= ) it is the
TCPIP address of the host no more, no less, either numberically or
as a host name to be resolved! If you need to specify other than the
default of Display 0 or Screen 0 then you add /screen=number
or /display=number or both. Adding :0.0 as you did above is plan 
wrong and does nothing! 

$ set display/create/transport=tcpip/node=172.21.100.125/display=0 -
/screen=0


