merchantability. Given the amount of time wasted in rebooting, crashing,
rebooting, buggered files and re-installing, people all over, in
commercial business and government are doing more futzing around with the
OS and Applications or Microsoft than they are spending in productive
work. This is probably why the worlds economy has gone for such a crap the
past 8 years or so. We are less productive with MS products than we were
with mid-size or main-frame systems. This all translates to financial
waste, loss and thus the downsizing syndrome of so many businesses over
the past 8 years. You'd think some senior exec's at some firms would wake
up and realize that the employee base does not need a real "All seeing all
powerfull, Bells and Whistles" Word processor on every desk. Heck, most
people only edit rudimentary text files. I really don't need the Exchange
stuff, with pretty pictures and font sizes and colours and all. It is a
collosal expenditure on overkill, resulting in a huge consumption of
peoples potential productive time.

