I've run into some SCSI related issues with a VAXstation 3100/30.

I just acquired a Western Digital 540 MB SCSI drive.  I pulled out
a 54 MB RZ22 disk and put in the WD 540.  The system picked it up no 
problem (console mode), did a low level "format"  (TEST 75) which 
completed successfully.  I turned the machine off, and left it for 
about 24 hours.  Upon booting it again, it comes up with SCSI errors;
the console boot report is as follows:

---------------------------------------------------------------
KA42-A V1.3

F...E...D...C...B...A...9...8...7...6?..5...4_..3_..2_..1...

?? 6  00A0  0000.5310
.>>>
---------------------------------------------------------------

I thought this was strange whereas it worked fine yesterday, so I did 
a "TEST 50", which came up with the following (I'm listing the full
output for completeness, note the SCSI-A section):

---------------------------------------------------------------
KA42-A  V1.3
ID 08-00-2B-10-70-D8

   MONO		0000.0001
   CLK		0000.0001
   NVR		0000.0001
   DZ		0000.0001
      00000001 00000001 00000001 00000001 00000001 043D12A0
   MEM
      01400000
   MM		0000.0001
   FP		0000.0001
   IT		0000.0001
   STRG-1	7777.0001  V1.30
      00000000 00000000 FFFFFFFF 00000000
?? SCSI-A	0000.5310  V1.30
      FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFFFF FFFFFF03
FFFFFFFF
   SYS		0000.0001
   NI		0100.0001
.>>>
---------------------------------------------------------------

I finally tried a "TEST 6", which came back with:

.>>> TEST 6

6?..
 84 FAIL
.>>>

...Which is pretty much what I expected.  A "SHOW DEV" only 
comes up with the ethernet adapter and the floppy drive; no 
SCSI devices are visible at all.

If anyone could give me some insight as to what's going on
with the SCSI device (or what I broke!), it would be greatly
appreciated.

Thanks,

Peter
