Phillip Helbig wrote:
> 

> What is the oldest VMS VAX version supported for clustering with VMS
> 7.1 ALPHA?
> 
Check the 7.1 release notes.  It is VERY impartant that you install
h3 patch to your VAX to prevent disk corruption.

> Can the two VAX machines share a system disk, or does each machine
> have to have some (perhaps minimal) system disk of its own?
> 
A VAX cannot boot the Alpha system, but you could have both systems
exist seperately on your Alpha disks.

> Which machine should be the main cluster machine?
> 
The fastest!  It is my understanding that some operations are sequential
in a cluster such that your fast Alpha may have to sit idle waiting for
your VAX.  Therefore if you add a very slow machine to a fast machine,
the net speed will be slower.  The VAX may drag down the performance
of the Alpha substantially.

Ray T.



