According to my VS3100 manual, the error code 0000.5310 on the SCSI-A test
indicates that the problem is on the system module *and* the problem is not
on the system module.  Make of that what you will.

What happens if you disconnect this new drive and put the RZ22 back in ?
You may at least then have some confidence that the SCSI controller isn't
up the creek (or sadly not).

Incidentally, you're the second person hereabouts who has used the TEST
utility to run a low-level format on a SCSI disk, and then had problems.
I was under the impression that this isn't generally necessary, no matter
what machine the disk was originally used in, and should be a last-resort
activity when all other attempts to get a disk working had failed.  The
Microvax FAQ advises that this could result in an unusable disk...

