In article <34F97C08.77BA53AF@acd.net>, "James D. McComb" <mccomb.james@acd.net> writes:
:I am installing a RZ28 in my VS3100/76.  The drive shows on the bus and
:I was able to backup the image of my RZ26 on to it.
:
:The probem is that it won't boot.  Comes back and says 'no such file'.
:
:Any ideas?

  This is (briefly) covered in the OpenVMS FAQ, and has been mentioned
  in various newsgroup postings before.

  No member of the VAXstation 3100 series can reliably bootstrap from a
  system disk larger than 1.073 GB -- this is a hard and permanent limit
  of the console PROM program used in this series of VAX systems.

  Those VAXstation 3100 series systems that do (appear to) successfully
  bootstrap with disks larger than 1.073 GB are merely operating at the
  risk of severe disk data corruptions at an unspecified future time.

  For details, search the http://www.dejanews.com/ archives for previous
  postings using a"1.073" or some such search string -- I have posted
  details of what happens and why to this newsgroup and/or to the
  comp.os.vms newsgroup.

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
