Mark & Suzanne (remove the dot to reply) wrote:
> 
> Philip Nasadowski wrote:
> but
> > am at a loss as to how to get this mess set up.  I've tried a few
> > mutations of SET DISPLAY, but when i try to run anything, I get an error
> > message : can't open display.  Is there some way to set this up right, or
> > should get a new hobby? ;)
> 
> $ set display/create/transport=tcpip/host=172.21.100.125
> $ show display
> $ create term
> You should get the decterm on the display of 172.21.100.125
> It may get rejected by the security on the display. Depending upon
> what 172.21.100.125 is there will be different ways to configure
> display security.

Depending on the X device you're using you may need to add ":0" or
":0.0" to the host specification.  Eg:

 $ set display/create/transport=tcpip/host=172.21.100.125:0.0

Note that you can use host names instead of ip addresses.
 
> Also the obvious things that you have a TCP stack install and working
> on the VMS host and that ucx loop 172.21.100.125 says your alive
> or what every equiv command that you tcpip stack uses

IIRC, the original message referred to using telnet to connect to
the VAX so that would seem to imply that a tcpip stack was up and
working.  For MultiNet, the command to use is

  $ mu x11debug

If you continue having problems you might want to post to
comp.os.vms where lots of VMS folks hang out.

Hth,
