mustang@ucc.gu.uwa.edu.au wrote:
> 
> Hi - got a 3000/300L here with 4 SIMMs in it.
> Not so strange, since Alphas use a 128-bit interleave AFAIK, but
> the SIMMs are single sided, and two-chip. That seems a little odd to me.

You are right. You can probably look up the chips through altavista
and find out what those simms really are.

> 
> It won't fire up, neither talking to a VRT16 or to a VT-320 off the
> serial port. The Blinkenlichts on the RHS of the board (facing the front)
> all light up on application of power, and settle into a pattern thus:
> 11111010, i.e. bank 11 is all on, and bank 12 shows on/off/on/off.

Well 0xF0 - 0xFF  indicates a failure of the srom load. No wonder if
you don't have any real ram.

> 
> Can anyone suggest where to go from here?
> 

1. Get a couple of 72 pin, true parity, 70ns 8 meg or 32 meg industry
standard simms. put them in the 1st  pair of slots and see if you
pass diags.

2. Order the "DEC 3000 Model 300/300L AXP Hardware Reference Guide"
Part num. EK-PELCN-OG. B01

